    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Major depressive disorder, single episode, moderate (F32.1)</content>. PHQ-9 8, 53 percent below baseline, and GDS-15 4: a response, not yet remission, after seven weeks of combined sertraline and IPT. No side effects; no suicidal thoughts. [S]<list><item>Continue sertraline 50 mg and weekly IPT.</item><item>Review in four weeks, at about twelve weeks of treatment; if the PHQ-9 is still 5 or more, increase sertraline to 75 mg.</item><item>Once in remission, continue sertraline for at least six to twelve months before a slow taper.</item><item>Safety plan kept; 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline confirmed.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Chronic insomnia comorbid with depression (G47.00)</content>. Insomnia Severity Index 11, down from 19. [S]<list><item>Widen the sleep window by another 15 minutes.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Partial loss of teeth with an ill-fitting partial denture (K08.409)</content>. New denture to be fitted next week. [S]<list><item>Dietitian review of protein and energy intake after the denture is fitted.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Fall risk (Z91.81)</content>. No falls; Timed Up and Go 10 seconds. The DXA ordered at the wellness visit has not yet been done. [S]<list><item>DXA booked for next week.</item><item>Continue the balance class.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>PHQ-9</td><td>Baseline, then at least monthly during acute treatment; every 2 to 4 weeks in continuation</td><td>Completed today</td><td>8, down from 17 (53 percent): response; remission is PHQ-9 below 5</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>GDS-15</td><td>Baseline and to monitor response in adults 65 or older (monthly here)</td><td>Completed today</td><td>4, below the cutoff of 5</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Suicide risk reassessment (C-SSRS Since Last Visit and PHQ-9 item 9)</td><td>Every visit during active treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No suicidal thoughts, intent, plan, or behavior; PHQ-9 item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Sodium on an SSRI</td><td>After starting, after dose increases, and with symptoms</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>136 mmol/L four weeks after starting; no dose change and no confusion, nausea, or unsteadiness</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Adherence and adverse-effect review</td><td>Every visit during active treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No missed doses; no side effects</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Interpersonal psychotherapy</td><td>Weekly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Six sessions; grief focus</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight and nutrition</td><td>Every visit while weight is below her usual</td><td>Completed today</td><td>53.4 kg, up 1.0 kg since the diagnosis visit; usual weight 55.9 kg</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Fall risk on an SSRI: orthostatic blood pressure, gait, and falls since the last visit</td><td>At baseline, after starting an SSRI, and with dose changes</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No falls; no orthostatic drop; Timed Up and Go 10 seconds</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>DXA of the hip and spine</td><td>Once for women 65 or older; ordered at the wellness visit</td><td>Due</td><td>Booked for next week; no result yet</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Sleep (CBT-I), activity, and social contact</td><td>Every visit during active treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Insomnia Severity Index 11; audiences, music, and friends resumed</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Lithium, anticonvulsant, or antipsychotic monitoring (levels, metabolic tests, AIMS)</td><td>Only on those drugs</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Treated with an SSRI only</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Medical causes of low mood and weight loss excluded by the second visit. Outcome by 2026-01-26: Blood count, metabolic panel, calcium, albumin, TSH, vitamin B12, folate, and MoCA normal; diphenhydramine stopped [S]</item><item>Response (PHQ-9 down by at least 50 percent) by twelve weeks of treatment, then remission (PHQ-9 below 5). In progress; target 2026-04-20 [S]</item><item>No passive or active suicidal thoughts. Outcome by 2026-01-26: Passive death wish at intake only; PHQ-9 item 9 scored 0 from the second visit [S]</item><item>Sleep at least six hours most nights without hypnotics. In progress; target 2026-04-20 [S]</item><item>Weight back to at least 55 kg, with a comfortable denture. In progress; target 2026-06-15 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: APA Clinical Practice Guideline for the Treatment of Depression Across Three Age Cohorts (2019); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Major Depressive Disorder (2022); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (2026); American Geriatrics Society 2023 Updated AGS Beers Criteria for Potentially Inappropriate Medication Use in Older Adults (2023); Management of Chronic Insomnia Disorder in Adults: A Clinical Practice Guideline From the American College of Physicians (2016); Osteoporosis to Prevent Fractures: Screening (2025)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Depression review in four weeks, at about twelve weeks of treatment. [S]</paragraph></text>

